#guide The guide becomes the left pane in Macro as in Files and Flow, and the overview card shrinks to a bar that expands on demand.
#risk low Renderer-only change to one pane; no data, parsing or record format is touched, and the unguided review is unchanged.
#gstep careful Split the overview card into a bar and a foldable rest
#gwhy Everything else leans on this markup: the bar keeps id, state, title and View PR, and the rest hides behind a toggle whose default depends on the guide.
#ghunk src/renderer/lib/lanternprpanel.ts
#gpseudo the bar always shows number, state, title, View PR and the toggle
#gpseudo the rest of the card is hidden unless the card is open
#gpseudo the card is open by default only when the record has no guide
#gstep careful Host the guide in Macro and remember the card state
#gwhy Macro now draws the header plus the guide pane instead of the file list, and the toggle keeps one open or closed choice per pull request.
#ghunk src/renderer/lib/lanternview.ts
#gpseudo guide stops no longer exclude Macro, so stepping follows the guide there too
#gpseudo in Macro with a guide, the side pane is the header and the guide pane
#gpseudo toggling the card flips the stored choice for this pull request and redraws
#gstep skim Drop the reason under a step note
#gwhy A one-line change: the step note already explains the file, so the reason block is skipped when a note is shown.
#ghunk src/renderer/lib/lanternreview.ts
